<Site title="Follow a drop"><PageHeader title="Follow a drop" eyebrow="Explainer · water systems" description="How rainfall can become usable water—and why each step needs its own observation." crumbs={[{label:'Understand',href:'/understand/'},{label:'Follow a drop'}]} /><div class="shell page-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">Question</p><h2>Can rain tell us what reaches a tap?</h2><p>Only indirectly. Rain falls over a catchment, some moves into rivers or aquifers, some is stored or withdrawn, and some is treated and distributed. Each route depends on place, infrastructure, timing and management.</p><figure class="figure"><div class="path-flow" role="img" aria-label="Conceptual chain: rain, catchment, storage or aquifer, treatment and distribution, household"><span>Rain<br /><small>IMD observation</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Catchment<br /><small>Boundary and runoff</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Storage or aquifer<br /><small>Usable quantity</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Distribution<br /><small>Service and quality</small></span></div><figcaption>Conceptual diagram; arrows do not assert a measured connection for any place. Local sources and transfer records are needed.</figcaption></figure><h2>Where the chain can break</h2><p>Rainfall may be intense but short; a reservoir may be outside the administrative district it serves; groundwater observations can lag; a distribution network can lose water or interrupt service. None of these links can be filled from a rainfall anomaly alone.</p><h2>What would support a local answer?</h2><p>A dated IMD rain series over the relevant catchment, a reviewed source map, stable reservoir or well observations, utility production and service logs, and local quality tests. We currently publish no place-specific chain that meets all of those checks.</p><div class="note"><strong>What this does not tell us</strong><p>This diagram does not classify drought, safe water, household shortage or current risk.</p></div></article><aside><p class="eyebrow">Inspect further</p><a href={url('/basins/')}>Basin context</a><a href={url('/explore/')}>Approved observations</a><a href={url('/methodology/')}>Methods and limits</a><a href={url('/sources/imd_current/')}>IMD rainfall source lead</a></aside></div></Site>
